WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.010
Luke dates John the Baptist's
preaching by an emperor's reign:

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.110
the fifteenth year of Tiberius Caesar.

3
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:10.450
His family line for Jesus
runs back past Abraham,

4
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.310
all the way to Adam.

5
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.970
And his second volume, Acts,
ends with Paul preaching in Rome.

6
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:22.320
So did Luke write plain history, or a
plan of God stretching from Adam all the

7
00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.870
way to Rome?

8
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.640
In this mission, you'll follow Luke's map,

9
00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:30.720
from Galilee to Jerusalem and
out to the ends of the earth.

10
00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:36.160
Then you'll weigh up what his claims about
salvation mean alongside other religions.

11
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.440
Your mission: weigh up
how Luke tells history,

12
00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.560
from Adam all the way to Rome.
